Week 3 — Data Preparation

Coordinate Reference System (CRS)

The data was reprojected from EPSG:4326 (WGS 84) to EPSG:32632 (WGS 84 / UTM Zone 32N). EPSG:32632 uses metres and is suitable for spatial analysis in the Kaduna North study area.

Data Reprojected and Clipped

The datasets were reprojected to EPSG:32632 and clipped using the Kaduna North Boundary.

The final analysis-ready GeoPackage contains:

* Highway_KadunaNorth — 3,540 features
* Waterbodies_KadunaNorth — 38 features

The Waterways dataset had 3 point features and was flagged for review. The Buildings dataset had 94,254 features but was not included in the final lightweight GeoPackage because of file-size constraints.

Five Quality Checks

1. CRS Check: All prepared layers use EPSG:32632. Pass.
2. Geometry Type Check: Highways are lines, Waterbodies are polygons, Waterways are points, and Buildings are multipolygons. Waterways was flagged for review because it is represented as points.
3. Feature Count Check: Feature counts were recorded for each prepared dataset. Pass.
4. Geometry Validity Check: QGIS Check Validity found 0 invalid geometries in the prepared datasets. Pass.
5. Study Area/Clipping Check: The clipped features were checked against the Kaduna North Boundary and were found to be within the study area. Pass.

Problems Found

The Waterways dataset was represented as point geometry and was flagged for review. No invalid geometries were found.

The Buildings dataset was excluded from the final lightweight GeoPackage because the complete GeoPackage exceeded the GitHub web-upload size limit.

Analysis-Ready File

The final analysis-ready GeoPackage is:

Kaduna_North_Analysis_Ready_Final.gpkg

It contains the clipped Highway and Waterbodies layers for the Kaduna North study area.
